Subject: [PATCH v7 4/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Sync the list both ways with
 Fastmail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: llrnrlvxupkmxyzxwrttskqynyvozqus
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:30:05 +0000

A one-way fetch makes lab-mail a copy of Fastmail. A move or
deletion made on lab-mail never reaches Fastmail, and one made on
Fastmail never reaches lab-mail. Syncing both ways, with Archive
beside lists, lets either side change the list while Fastmail still
keeps every message.

- mbsync syncs lists and Archive both ways, but never expunges or
  removes. A message expunged on one side is only marked \Deleted on
  the other.
- Dovecot creates Archive, marked \Archive.
- The fetch job becomes the sync job, with its own log and stamp.
